@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="py-4">
    <h1 class="display-6">WorkMvc</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        ASP.NET Core MVC client for the REST vs GraphQL Proof of Concept. This app never talks
        to MongoDB directly - every page is rendered from data fetched over HTTP from either
        the .NET backend (port 5000) or the Node.js backend (port 4000), using either their
        REST API or their GraphQL API.
    </p>

    <h5>How to switch backend/mode</h5>
    <p>
        Append <code>?mode=rest|graphql&amp;backend=dotnet|node</code> to any URL, or use the
        switch buttons shown on every data page. The choice sticks (via a cookie) as you
        navigate.
    </p>

    <h5>Where to look</h5>
    <ul>
        <li><a asp-controller="Customer" asp-action="Index">Customers</a> - list, then drill into a customer's projects</li>
        <li><a asp-controller="Task" asp-action="Index">Tasks</a> - filterable task list with assigned user + tags</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-muted">
        Try Customer &rarr; Project (nested Tasks/Teams) &rarr; Task (AssignedUser/Tags/Comments) in both
        REST and GraphQL mode and compare the "backend HTTP calls" counter shown at the top of each page.
    </p>
</div>
